			<div class="content" id="post-content-4302949">
									

<p>So we've got an alternate dimension Foundation's article, and a creepy looking image to greet us right off the bat. Interesting premise.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Object Class: Spiritual</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Whelp. But ultimately this is just a classification and doesn't do much from a literary standpoint so, honestly, it counts neither towards or against the overall quality, despite what some may say.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCPF-LZPP87 is noticeably more loosely-organized and small-scale. Documentation as a result is rough and prone to inconsistencies in formatting and tone.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This, however, does work against the overall quality. This is what's known in the industry as 'author preemption.' Pretty much, the author steps into the work and talks directly to the reader asking them to forgive something that they're about to see. In this case, the author steps in and tells us that clinical tone, formatting and so on is inconsistent but lol don't worry its because alternate universe. Generally speaking, it's not a good sign to see inconsistent writing acknowledged by the author before we even begin reading the primary story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rosie: Stay out of this heretics, this is far beyond your udderstanding [sic].</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Grammatically incorrect. There should be a comma after 'this' since heretics are the receivers of that command. Beyond that, it's really difficult to take any antagonistic force seriously when they start spinning out puns. But like the object class, characterization is characterization. My dislike of puns is minor in comparison to:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(Through teeth.) Shut up.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I know that we should be ignoring 'inconsistent' tone thanks to the disclaimer but imagine the person who watched the magicamera footage tasked to record this important incident hearing this and going 'I'm gonna describe this creatively.'</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Daisy's abdominal mouth snaps at the book in M9-2's hand. As he attempts to pludge his sword into the mouth, a large spike of calcified rock extends from the mouth, destabilizing the sword and causing it to demanifest. M9-2 grabs Daisy by the mouth's teeth and throws her against the wall, damaging it. He kicks Daisy in the gut several more times, and the wall cracks further.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
<p>Plunge is spelled incorrectly. The sarcastic banter from the task force members, the pun/mustache-twirling pun cultists and the purely informal, action-adventure narration prose combines into a chunk of reading that is not just wholly uninteresting, but also gives off the impression that we are expected to forgive mistake after mistake (some of which include basic grammar and spelling) because this is an alternate universe and because the author said to not mind these.</p>
<p>-1</p>

							</div>

								
