			<div class="content" id="post-content-4303913">
									

<blockquote>
<p>This is the proof that the milk meme has been dried up.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To be fair, I don't think Laneous or Clem or I ever decided to write milk-related articles in service of a meme. I don't know where that observation came from but it's horribly simplistic, and I'm not quite sure what it means exactly from a critical standpoint. If your assertion is that this article is <em>for a meme</em>, it ignores the sheer amount of creativity put into this particular article <em>apart</em> from milk.</p>
<p>I can't deny that SCP-4487 should have gotten a lot more crit and feedback &#8212; for both its narrative structure and core concept &#8212; than what it received, and ought to have some further polishing based on the criticisms mentioned this discussion. But I think what was written here is really, genuinely imaginative, even if it isn't executed as well as it could have been.</p>
<p>At the same time, I'll point out that criticizing this article for supposedly not achieving what another article did achieve is missing the point. This article's content should be scrutinized on its own merits, not in comparison to something else.</p>

